AUDIO: 'the team has published a chart that puts it ahead of Jeff in several public tests. But there is also a test where she gets less than half of what Jeff gets. And a language where she got 0%'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'correct, while being 95% confident . I will go into both details. So, Jeff was created by a company founded by Diogo Almeida, who worked on ChatGPT at'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'OpenAI. Type-Safe calls this the system one model. System one is a quick intuitive conclusion that you make without much thought. System two is slow, careful reasoning. The Chat model and the reasoning model'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are on the system two side. They write token by token, and each word waits for the one before it. Jeff sits on the side of the system. She doesn\'t write anything.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You provide it with some state, such as an email, support request, or JSON object plus questions with fixed answers. It returns answers with added probabilities. Without'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a sentence, without analysis. In fact, most decisions within a business are small. Which team receives this request? Is this login notification real? Should this prospect go to'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sales today or next week? Many companies still send them to the big chat model. Jeff fixes this, but he charges 4.2 cents per million input tokens, and it\'s a private API. You can\'t'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'download it or run it on your own server, which is a real problem if your data can\'t leave the building. Leah fills this gap. It\'s from a small team, and it\'s licensed under the'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Apache 2.0 license, so you can use it commercially, modify it, and host it anywhere you want . On the GitHub page, it\'s called a multilingual non-autoaggressive system with a single decision-making mechanism.'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Non-autoaggressive simply means that it doesn\'t generate one word after another. He reads everything once and gives an answer. Leah is built on an encoder, not a chat model. The main checkpoint'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uses a state-of-the-art BERT with 421 million parameters . When you ask a multiple- choice question, each possible answer gets its own marker in the input. The model reads'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the question, options, and your text together in both directions. Each marker is then given a score. These estimates become probabilities. Your answer can only be one of the options you have already'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'given her. So, a made-up category or corrupted JSON simply cannot occur. This does not mean that the answer is always correct. This means that your code can always use it. And there are'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'three types of questions. And Leia uses the same name as Jev. Choice selects one label from the list, such as billing , technical issues, or sales. Score places something on a scale, such as'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'frustration, from zero to two. And null, which is a yes or no question that returns a probability between one and zero. You can submit multiple questions in a single call, and they are all completed in'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one pass. Both Jev and Leia say they are trained in RLCD, which stands for Reinforcement Learning for Calibrated Decision. If you reward'

[03:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the model only for correctness, it will learn to give every answer with 100% confidence, even if it is a guess. Layer reward comes from a correct scoring rule, where a model only gets the best score when its'

[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'probabilities are fair. So when it shows 80%, it should be correct about 80% of the time in many cases. There is also a small action or escalation that'

[04:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'teaches when to act independently and when to delegate tasks to a person. Layer comes in three control points. The base model is English, which has a context of 515'

[04:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tokens. The multilingual Layer uses a smaller encoder, covers over 100 languages, has a context of 124 tokens, and is about twice as fast. The Layer type solution is fine-'

